<p id="p1.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="p1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:144%;">Supplementary Material</span></p>
</div>
  
</div>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section supplements Sec. 4.1 with more details of our experiments.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Datasets.</span>
We report the dataset details in <a href="#S6.T2" title="In 6 Experimental Details ‣ Fisheye3R: Adapting Unified 3D Feed-Forward Foundation Models to Fisheye Lenses" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
For training with perspective data, we adopt the training split of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite> on these 6 datasets.
For training with fisheye data, we randomly select 30 scenes from ASE and 6 scenes from KITTI360 for <span id="S6.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SL+</span> learning.
For evaluation, we use the test split of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite> from ScanNet++, all the scenes from ADT, and 3 scenes from KITTI360.
Train-test split is enforced at the scene level to ensure no test sequence is seen by the model during training.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sequence sampling.</span>
The sampling scheme roughly follows <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>.
The sequence length is randomly sampled from 2–24 images per sequence during training, and from 4, 8, 16, and 32 during evaluation.
A pairwise covisibility matrix is pre-computed for each scene based on the ground-truth depth maps beforehand for all datasets except KITTI360 with extra-long sequences, i.e., from each source image, the percentage of its pixels visible from each target image is calculated.
Then, with the first reference frame selected randomly from a scene, and the remaining frames are added incrementally by including images with at least 25% pixels covisible from any sampled images.
For KITTI360, due to its large number of frames per scene, we randomly sample the remaining frames uniformly from an interval centered at the first frame, with the frames ordered by their timestamps.
During training, we set a maximum number of images per GPU to 24, thus equivalently 1–12 sequences per GPU, depending on the sampled sequence length.
With 4 GPUs for training, the model is trained by an effective batch of 4–48 sequences per iteration.
During evaluation, we sample 10, 1, and 100 sequences from each scene in ScanNet++, ADT, and KITTI360 respectively, with a total of 300, 236, and 300 test sequences from the three datasets.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Image processing.</span>
Training augmentations include random resizing, cropping, color jittering, gray-scale conversion, and Gaussian blur.
Images are resized such that the longer edge is 518 pixels, while the shorter edge is adjusted to the nearest multiple of 14 that preserves the aspect ratio.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Distortion synthesis.</span>
We apply the Kannala-Brandt distortion model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> to synthesize varying fisheye distortions from perspective images.
Specifically, each 3D ray direction <math id="S6.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{d}=(x,y,z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒅</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{d}=(x,y,z)</annotation></semantics></math> is mapped to the image plane by first computing the incident angle</p>
<table id="S6.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=\arctan\frac{\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}}}{z}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arctan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mi>z</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=\arctan\frac{\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}}}{z},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p5.2" class="ltx_p">and modeling the radial distance from the principal point as a polynomial of <math id="S6.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S6.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\theta)=\theta+k_{1}\theta^{3}+k_{2}\theta^{5}+k_{3}\theta^{7}+k_{4}\theta^{9}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>7</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>9</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\theta)=\theta+k_{1}\theta^{3}+k_{2}\theta^{5}+k_{3}\theta^{7}+k_{4}\theta^{9},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p5.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1},k_{2},k_{3},k_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1},k_{2},k_{3},k_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> are distortion coefficients.
The final corresponding pixel coordinates <math id="S6.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u,v)</annotation></semantics></math> in the fisheye image are given by</p>
<table id="S6.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=f_{x}\frac{x}{\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}}}r(\theta)+c_{x},\qquad v=f_{y}\frac{y}{\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}}}r(\theta)+c_{y}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=f_{x}\frac{x}{\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}}}r(\theta)+c_{x},\qquad v=f_{y}\frac{y}{\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}}}r(\theta)+c_{y},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p5.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f_{x},f_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f_{x},f_{y})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c_{x},c_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c_{x},c_{y})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the focal lengths and the principal point.
During training, we randomly set the focal length to [1, 1.2] times the original perspective focal length and shift the principal point by [-10, 10] pixels from the original principal point, with coefficients being uniformly sampled from <math id="S6.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1},k_{2},k_{3}\in(-0.5,0.5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1},k_{2},k_{3}\in(-0.5,0.5)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{4}\in(-0.05,0.05)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.05</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{4}\in(-0.05,0.05)</annotation></semantics></math> to synthesize different distortions.
For mixture training with both camera types, each sequence is randomly selected to be either fully perspective, fully fisheye, or hybrid.
For a hybrid sequence, each frame has a 0.5 probability of being distorted.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T2" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S6.T2.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S6.T2.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T2.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Split</span></th>
<th id="S6.T2.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T2.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Dataset</span></th>
<th id="S6.T2.3.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T2.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Type</span></th>
<th id="S6.T2.3.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T2.3.1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Environment</span></th>
<th id="S6.T2.3.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T2.3.1.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Scenes</span></th>
<th id="S6.T2.3.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T2.3.1.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Images/Scene</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S6.T2.3.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T2.3.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" rowspan="6"><span id="S6.T2.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
<span id="S6.T2.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block">
<span id="S6.T2.3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Train</span>
<span id="S6.T2.3.2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_p">(Perspective)</span>
</span></span></td>
<td id="S6.T2.3.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T2.3.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">ScanNet++ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite></span></td>
<td id="S6.T2.3.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T2.3.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Real</span></td>
<td id="S6.T2.3.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T2.3.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Indoor</span></td>
<td id="S6.T2.3.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T2.3.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">896</span></td>
<td id="S6.T2.3.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T2.3.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">1059.6</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T2.3.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T2.3.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r"><span id="S6.T2.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">MegaDepth <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite></span></td>
